		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  event trigger ddl_command_end ne rapporte pas les ordres DROP]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=30493#p30493"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>D&#039;après la documentation :</p><div class="quotebox"><blockquote><div><p>To list the objects that have been dropped, use the set-returning function pg_event_trigger_dropped_objects() from the sql_drop event trigger code (see Section 9.28). Note that the trigger is executed after the objects have been deleted from the system catalogs, so it&#039;s not possible to look them up anymore.</p></div></blockquote></div>]]></content>
